    "topic_id": 2625867,
    "poster_id": 305311,
    "post_rendered": "For each prime <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" >,</span> construct a graph <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de6691da5a300cd0e228a7e5accaed448dacb71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" > on <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f457fa9dd1fb03cd24017aaa63e0546abe4be334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,\\ldots p\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" >,</span> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebce927784f9982450c5d86c7965ea5c0ca609ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\neq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" > are adjacent if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" > divides <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369f3e5425aea15b58413c96e70f93cc3c0142cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m^{2} + 1-n)(n^{2} + 1-m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"21\" >.</span> Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de6691da5a300cd0e228a7e5accaed448dacb71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" > is disconnected for infinitely many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" >",
    "post_canonical": "For each prime $p$, construct a graph $G_p$ on $\\{1,2,\\ldots p\\}$, where $m\\neq n$ are adjacent if and only if $p$ divides $(m^{2} + 1-n)(n^{2} + 1-m)$. Prove that $G_p$ is disconnected for infinitely many $p$",
    "username": "Eyed",
