   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 22698213,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 2625881,
    "poster_id": 611385,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\"  width=\"57\" height=\"13\" > be a convex quadrilateral with <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a828313726409cdb0999f73fc6a2aa58ffab3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC&gt;90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"97\" height=\"13\" >,</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba45bca9408298d9867e9029be74a297da479a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDA&gt;90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b41724c795b202a3dd6d719de5c871fbd3d10ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB=\\angle BCD$\"  width=\"138\" height=\"13\" >.</span> Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > the reflections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > in lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\"  width=\"29\" height=\"12\" >,</span> respectively. Suppose that the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" > meet the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\"  width=\"29\" height=\"12\" > at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\"  width=\"12\" height=\"12\" >,</span> respectively. Prove that the circumcircles of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f28bcd8fa84d766ba3b082935f46dd918a918db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEK$\"  width=\"45\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904bd60ed06459a138982e61891a5fc66a1f74b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DFL$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"12\" > are tangent to each other.<br>\n<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d33f779984d42f36644413ff1aec410f51839f68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\emph{Slovakia}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Let $ABCD$ be a convex quadrilateral with $\\angle ABC>90$, $CDA>90$ and $\\angle DAB=\\angle BCD$. Denote by $E$ and $F$ the reflections of $A$ in lines $BC$ and $CD$, respectively. Suppose that the segments $AE$ and $AF$ meet the line $BD$ at $K$ and $L$, respectively. Prove that the circumcircles of triangles $BEK$ and $DFL$ are tangent to each other.\n\n$\\emph{Slovakia}$",
    "username": "trying_to_solve_br",
    "post_number": 1,
