    "post_rendered": "Prove:For all nonnegative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/984590c9b249e56c8368ea433b0c6e031ec06026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" > there is exactly one pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca10ffe3531cf1faf6222be7eac407c47bef878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" > of positive integers such that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cdd5872c9c37f3554e82c246140000d8a2348f3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2z=(m+n)^2-m-3n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"21\" >.</span>",
